<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Korean strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  Sentences use the formal polite style (합니다, requests with 하십시오), as Korean iOS system text does;
  buttons and labels are short nouns. Spacing follows the Korean standard rules; a counter joins its number ("3회").
  Korean has only the CLDR plural form "other".
-->
